      "rev_n_2_ff44b1_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_ff44b1_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_ff44b1",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in how the `count_ways` function updates the `total_niceness`. It should accumulate the niceness values for each subtree rather than just adding them directly. Additionally, the base case for the `dfs` function should handle cases where there are no neighbors, which currently isn't addressed.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_ff44b1_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9b1a9a8e25",
        "created_at": 1794506699.0723565
      },
      "rev_n_3_be2787_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_be2787_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_be2787",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Dynamic Programming with Bitmasking\n\nWe need to use dynamic programming with bitmasking to efficiently calculate the niceness for all possible colorings of the tree. For each node, maintain two states: the maximum distance between white vertices and the maximum distance between black vertices. Use bitwise operations to keep track of the current coloring and update the DP table accordingly. This approach ensures that we can handle the constraints effectively without running into performance issues.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_be2787_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ae300151e8",
        "created_at": 1794506747.2331545
      },
      "rev_n_4_6aff0f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_6aff0f_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_6aff0f",
        "thought_text": "Revisit the initialization of the DP table within the dfs function.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4236482014784927498",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506772.2068884
      },
      "rev_n_5_15d1f4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_15d1f4_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_15d1f4",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the calculation of the maximum distance for each color.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4236482014784927498",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506772.206911
      },
      "rev_n_6_8e1bee_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_8e1bee_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_8e1bee",
